David Damerell wrote:
> Quoting  James <james.kanze@gmail.com>:
> >Similar analysis could be done for each role.  For some
> >roles (ranger, wizard), the results are obvious, and do
> >favor ranged attacks.  For others (valkyrie, samari), I find
> >that the results favor melee.

> They favour melee in the sense that they'll end up doing more of it, but
> not in the sense that they shouldn't use ranged attacks "early and often".
> Valks can get that dagger skill up to Expert, in particular - the sooner
> the better.

That's a slightly different argument.  For most roles, I think,
it's worth getting the fighting skills you intend on using up as
high as you intend on getting them as early as possible.
(Spellcasting skills can often wait, since many roles won't be
able to learn any spells until much later anyway, until they get
experience and intelligence up.)

In the case of a legal Valk or Samurai, I still tend to push
long sword and two weapon up before daggers or bow (although I
want all three at expert).  Probably influenced by the fact that
I know they'll be wielding Excalibur fairly early (and the fact
that long swords are frequent enough that they'll probably be
two weaponing it)---you're probably right that getting the
ranged weapon up there before two-weaponing is probably a good
idea.

